                <pb facs="0568" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/707: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-18T19:00:00+08:00">December 18, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 18—2 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1167. My 1160, December 18, 11 a.m. Following from American Consul, Harbin:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 18, 11 a.m. International car has been ordered to return to
                            Buketu by the Chinese military command. It appears that Red Mongol
                            detachment started an encircling movement which forced Chinese military
                            to withdraw on the [railway?] to Mientuho, possibly to Buketu.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
